00:36:43.345 --> 00:36:45.220
So thank you, Dmitry.

00:36:45.220 --> 00:36:47.990
The reason I'm here is because
if you leave this room--

00:36:47.990 --> 00:36:49.890
and I'm hoping you
do after we are done.

00:36:49.890 --> 00:36:51.740
But when you leave
this room, you

00:36:51.740 --> 00:36:53.490
leave with four key takeaways.

00:36:53.490 --> 00:36:58.230
First, our Global Load Balancing
is software-defined load

00:36:58.230 --> 00:37:00.250
balancing for cloud scale.

00:37:00.250 --> 00:37:02.880
It uses state-of-the-art
software-defined technologies

00:37:02.880 --> 00:37:05.360
and distributive systems
technologies along with,

00:37:05.360 --> 00:37:08.240
of course, Google's
global network.

00:37:08.240 --> 00:37:11.350
The second one is you
can deliver your services

00:37:11.350 --> 00:37:15.410
across the globe with a
single anycast front-end VIP.

00:37:15.410 --> 00:37:18.526
You will not find this in
any other cloud provider.

00:37:18.526 --> 00:37:22.450
Third, it will deliver
high performance,

00:37:22.450 --> 00:37:25.990
low latency, and seamless
scaling, or rather,

00:37:25.990 --> 00:37:28.380
seamless autoscaling
for all your services.

00:37:28.380 --> 00:37:31.080
And lastly, you can
optimize your delivery

00:37:31.080 --> 00:37:35.970
across the globe using three
things-- Cloud CDN, CDN

00:37:35.970 --> 00:37:38.760
Interconnect, and of course
Google's global network that

00:37:38.760 --> 00:37:40.800
enables all of this.

00:37:40.800 --> 00:37:43.370
So with that, I think we
come to the end of it.

00:37:43.370 --> 00:37:45.090
Feel free to get
any one of us if you

00:37:45.090 --> 00:37:46.920
have any further question.

00:37:46.920 --> 00:37:50.200
And with that, let's
conclude and say, scale on!

00:37:50.200 --> 00:37:51.000
Thank you.

